1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,099
You type a question into

2
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:03,519
ChatGPT, and a second later

3
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:05,499
an answer starts appearing, word

4
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:06,100
by word.

5
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:07,980
But where is it coming from?

6
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:09,860
There's no person typing.

7
00:00:10,580 --> 00:00:11,860
It isn't copying a webpage.

8
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:14,379
Most of the time, it isn't

9
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:15,580
looking anything up at all.

10
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:17,779
So where does the answer come

11
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:18,140
from?

12
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:21,459
Quick test, finish this sentence

13
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:22,660
once upon A.

14
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:26,300
You said time, didn't you?

15
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,459
then you just did exactly what

16
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:29,620
ChatGPT does.

17
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:32,640
ChatGPT is a guessing machine.

18
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:35,079
It looks at the word so far and

19
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:36,599
guesses the most likely next

20
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:36,860
word.

21
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:39,260
It adds that word, looks again,

22
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:41,439
and guesses the next one, and

23
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:41,860
the next.

24
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:43,620
That's it.

25
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:45,739
Every answer it has ever given

26
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:47,519
you was built like that, one

27
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:48,380
guess at a time.

28
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:50,360
So three questions.

29
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:51,980
Guessing from what?

30
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:53,819
Why can't it count letters?

31
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:55,939
And why does the same question

32
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:56,940
get different answers?

33
00:00:57,700 --> 00:00:59,239
Question one, guessing from

34
00:00:59,240 --> 00:00:59,520
what?

35
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:01,759
You knew time because you've

36
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:03,320
heard that line 100 times.

37
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:05,820
ChatGPT learned the same way,

38
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:07,380
just on a giant scale.

39
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:09,499
Remember, fill in the blank

40
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:10,560
worksheets from school.

41
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:12,280
The cat sat on the blank.

42
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:13,760
That's its training.

43
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:15,980
It was shown a mountain of text,

44
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:18,339
books, websites, articles, with

45
00:01:18,340 --> 00:01:19,260
the next word hidden.

46
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:20,320
It guessed.

47
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:21,980
The guess was checked.

48
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:24,299
If it was wrong, it got adjusted

49
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:25,100
a tiny bit.

50
00:01:25,630 --> 00:01:27,960
Then again, billions of times.

51
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,520
Nobody gave it a list of facts.

52
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:32,679
It just got incredibly good at

53
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:33,000
blanks.

54
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:35,419
That's why this kind of AI is

55
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:36,540
called a language model.

56
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,639
Then people trained it some more

57
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:39,879
to answer like a helpful

58
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:40,340
assistant.

59
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,619
But underneath, it's still the

60
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:43,959
world's best fill in the blank

61
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:44,260
player.

62
00:01:44,967 --> 00:01:47,246
Question two, how many R's are

63
00:01:47,247 --> 00:01:47,787
in strawberry?

64
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:51,287
Three, but for a long time,

65
00:01:51,627 --> 00:01:53,426
ChatGPT would confidently say

66
00:01:53,427 --> 00:01:54,107
two.

67
00:01:55,087 --> 00:01:55,827
Here's why.

68
00:01:56,527 --> 00:01:57,846
I've been saying it guesses the

69
00:01:57,847 --> 00:01:58,427
next word.

70
00:01:58,987 --> 00:02:00,307
That was a little white lie.

71
00:02:00,947 --> 00:02:02,567
It doesn't see words or letters.

72
00:02:03,227 --> 00:02:04,747
It sees chunks called tokens.

73
00:02:05,567 --> 00:02:07,046
Your message gets chopped into

74
00:02:07,047 --> 00:02:09,226
pieces and each piece becomes a

75
00:02:09,227 --> 00:02:09,447
number.

76
00:02:10,567 --> 00:02:11,646
Strawberry might get chopped

77
00:02:11,647 --> 00:02:13,147
into three pieces like this.

78
00:02:13,867 --> 00:02:15,646
Now imagine I text you a

79
00:02:15,647 --> 00:02:17,706
strawberry emoji and ask how

80
00:02:17,707 --> 00:02:18,787
many R's are in it.

81
00:02:19,207 --> 00:02:20,446
The picture doesn't show any

82
00:02:20,447 --> 00:02:20,747
letters.

83
00:02:21,507 --> 00:02:22,546
You'd have to remember the

84
00:02:22,547 --> 00:02:22,887
spelling.

85
00:02:23,567 --> 00:02:25,107
That's ChatGPT's problem.

86
00:02:25,907 --> 00:02:27,606
Newer versions usually work

87
00:02:27,607 --> 00:02:29,006
around it by spelling the word

88
00:02:29,007 --> 00:02:29,567
out first.

89
00:02:30,187 --> 00:02:31,427
But the chunks are still there,

90
00:02:31,687 --> 00:02:33,306
so letter puzzles can still trip

91
00:02:33,307 --> 00:02:33,607
it up.

92
00:02:34,167 --> 00:02:36,366
Question three, ask the same

93
00:02:36,367 --> 00:02:38,326
question twice and you'll often

94
00:02:38,327 --> 00:02:39,547
get two different answers.

95
00:02:40,167 --> 00:02:40,487
Why?

96
00:02:41,147 --> 00:02:42,586
Because it doesn't always pick

97
00:02:42,587 --> 00:02:43,647
the single top guess.

98
00:02:44,727 --> 00:02:45,706
Think about your favorite

99
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:46,347
restaurant.

100
00:02:47,047 --> 00:02:48,867
Most days you order your usual.

101
00:02:49,527 --> 00:02:51,146
Some days you try the dish you

102
00:02:51,147 --> 00:02:51,887
almost ordered.

103
00:02:52,427 --> 00:02:53,966
The setting that controls this

104
00:02:53,967 --> 00:02:55,067
is called temperature.

105
00:02:56,207 --> 00:02:58,066
Turn it down and it orders the

106
00:02:58,067 --> 00:02:59,627
usual every single time.

107
00:03:00,047 --> 00:03:01,367
Safe but a bit boring.

108
00:03:01,967 --> 00:03:03,246
Turn it up and it gets

109
00:03:03,247 --> 00:03:03,787
adventurous.

110
00:03:04,527 --> 00:03:06,586
More creative and too far up it

111
00:03:06,587 --> 00:03:07,647
starts ordering nonsense.

112
00:03:08,567 --> 00:03:10,326
ChatGPT keeps it turned up a

113
00:03:10,327 --> 00:03:10,467
little.

114
00:03:11,147 --> 00:03:13,326
And once one word changes, every

115
00:03:13,327 --> 00:03:14,787
guess after it changes too.

116
00:03:15,433 --> 00:03:16,573
So put it all together.

117
00:03:17,293 --> 00:03:18,872
Your message gets chopped into

118
00:03:18,873 --> 00:03:19,373
tokens.

119
00:03:20,273 --> 00:03:22,032
ChatGPT guesses the next one

120
00:03:22,033 --> 00:03:23,832
from patterns in a mountain of

121
00:03:23,833 --> 00:03:24,193
text.

122
00:03:24,973 --> 00:03:25,892
Picks one with a little

123
00:03:25,893 --> 00:03:26,533
randomness.

124
00:03:27,273 --> 00:03:29,233
Adds it and guesses again.

125
00:03:30,253 --> 00:03:31,612
There's no finished answer

126
00:03:31,613 --> 00:03:32,413
waiting somewhere.

127
00:03:32,853 --> 00:03:34,513
It's built one guess at a time,

128
00:03:34,793 --> 00:03:36,352
the same way you finished once

129
00:03:36,353 --> 00:03:36,953
upon A.

130
00:03:37,813 --> 00:03:39,233
And notice what it's guessing.

131
00:03:40,773 --> 00:03:42,972
What sounds right, not what is

132
00:03:42,973 --> 00:03:43,313
right.

133
00:03:44,193 --> 00:03:46,092
Most of the time, those are the

134
00:03:46,093 --> 00:03:46,633
same thing.

135
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:48,620
But sometimes they're not.

136
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:50,559
And that's when AI makes

137
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:51,919
something up, with total

138
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:52,440
confidence.

139
00:03:53,160 --> 00:03:54,899
It's called a hallucination, and

140
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:55,400
it's next.

141
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:58,359
Subscribe so you don't miss why

142
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:59,620
AI hallucinates.

143
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:01,300
And tell me in the comments,

144
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,799
what's the strangest thing an AI

145
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:04,880
has ever told you?
